course: dictionary
lesson: 3839
title: Fortunate: luck and having more
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Fortunate means lucky. When something good happens by chance, you were fortunate. «We were fortunate that the rain stopped just as the match began.» The rain stopping was not planned, so the word fortunate tells you luck played a part.
explain: The word can also mean having more good things, like money or comfort, than many people. «Help those less fortunate» means help people who have fewer good things than most of us. Here fortunate is about what a person has, not about chance.
explain: Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «She was fortunate enough to win a ticket» means she was lucky enough to win one. If you can swap in lucky and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Fortunate means lucky, or having something good happen to you by chance.
fact: Fortunate can also mean having more good things, like money or comfort, than many people.
fact: «Fortunate enough to» means lucky enough to, as in «fortunate enough to see the sea».
fact: «Less fortunate» describes people who have fewer good things, like money or comfort, than most people.
fact: «Less fortunate» is a gentle, polite way of talking about people who are poor, so it is not rude.
exercise: «We were fortunate that the bus was early.» What does fortunate mean here? | *Lucky, because something good happened by chance | Hungry after the journey | Angry about the bus | Tired from walking
exercise: A charity poster says «help those less fortunate». What does less fortunate mean? | *Having fewer good things, like money or comfort, than many people | Having more good things than most people | Asleep in class | Able to run very fast
exercise: Find and copy the word that means lucky in «She was fortunate enough to win the prize.» | prize | win | *fortunate | she
test: Maya says, «It was fortunate that the sun came out for our picnic.» What does fortunate tell you? | Maya was sad about the picnic | The sun was too hot to sit in | *Luck played a part, and the sun coming out was a good chance | The picnic was cancelled
test: Leo says «less fortunate» is rude. Is he right? | *No, it is a kind way to talk about people with fewer good things | Yes, it means very happy | No, it means very tall | Yes, it always means rude
exam: Which sentence uses fortunate to mean lucky? | Fortunate is a number on the clock | The fortunate dog ran across the road | *We were fortunate that the ferry was not cancelled | The table was fortunate and made of oak
